Mia Wang: Quick UX poll: compact left nav + deep link — keep a slim breadcrumb or rely on header workspace? noticed filters drop with short links :thinking_face:
Omar Khan: Slim breadcrumb. Landing context matters. If hidden, header must show workspace and be keyboard-focusable.
Jamie Lee: We should choose a canonical URL: `/w/:ws/...` and client-rewrite `/models/:id?ws=` to that on first load to avoid hydration surprises.
Nora Patel: A11y: crumbs need nav landmark, `aria-current="page"` on active, and truncated text must include `aria-label`. Mobile should open an accessible sheet with actions.
navbot: Draft spec: https://redwood.design/ux/mini-crumbs  includes canary plan and a11y checklist.
Jamie Lee: Router snippet for migration:
```
if (location.search.includes('ws=') && location.pathname.startsWith('/models/')) {
  const p = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
  const ws = p.get('ws');
  const id = location.pathname.split('/').pop();
  history.replaceState({}, '', `/w/${ws}/models/${id}` + location.search);
  telemetry.track('rewrite_ws_query');
}
```
Mia Wang: I'll update mocks with condensed crumbs + mobile sheet long-press behavior and tag @Nora for a11y review. Thanks!
